<section xml:id="sec_what-is-elec" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
	<title>What Is Electricity?</title>

	<outcomes xml:id="adapting-model-electricity">
	<title>Electricity</title>
	<ul>
		<li>
		<p>You now have an extensive physics model that encompasses many forces and their impact on translation, rotational, oscillatory, and wave motion.</p>
	</li>
	<li>
		<p>
			You will now explore a quantitative model for one of the most fundamental forces in nature: <alert>the electric force</alert>.
		</p>
	</li>
	<li>
		<p>
			In the next several chapters, you will see how the electric force fits into your existing physics model, and what new techniques will help you describe electricity.
		</p>
	</li>
</ul>
</outcomes>

<subsubsection>
		<title>Activities</title>
		<activity>
			<title>Electricity</title>
			<p>
			
			</p>
			  <p>Describe an instance in your everyday life when you have experienced a phenomenon related to electric charge or electricity.</p>
		</activity>
	</subsubsection>


		
